course: dictionary
lesson: 6707
title: One word, two meanings: odyssey
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and a capital letter can change which one you mean. Odyssey with a small o is a noun for any long, exciting journey full of adventures and difficulties. «Our journey to Granny's was a real odyssey.» The clues are a long trip with things going wrong, so you know it means a big adventure, not a poem.
explain: The Odyssey with a capital O is a name. It is an ancient Greek epic poem, said to be by Homer, about the hero Odysseus and his ten-year journey home after the Trojan War. Names of books, poems and films start with a capital letter. Look for the capital and the context before you decide which meaning you need.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the sentence is about a poem or a hero, you need the Odyssey. If it is about a trip or an experience, use a small o: odyssey, or odysseys in the plural.
fact: Odyssey (small o) means a long, exciting journey full of adventures and difficulties.
fact: The Odyssey (capital O) is an ancient Greek epic poem, said to be by Homer.
fact: The Odyssey tells of Odysseus and his ten-year journey home after the Trojan War.
fact: On his journey Odysseus meets the Cyclops and the Sirens, while Penelope waits for him at home.
fact: «Many everyday English words were born in these old stories: panic, odyssey, mentor, echo, cereal and even the month of January.»
exercise: «Our journey to Granny's took five hours, with a broken car and a lost map. It was a real odyssey.» What does odyssey mean here? | *A long, eventful journey full of difficulties | A small, quiet picnic in the park | A kind of cake from Greece | A poem about a dog
exercise: Which is the name of the ancient Greek poem, and so needs a capital letter? | *the Odyssey | odysseys | the odyssey | an odyssey
exercise: What did Odysseus do before his ten-year journey home? | Built a castle in the hills | Ate a feast with the Sirens | *Fought in the Trojan War | Won a race in ancient Greece
test: Which character in the Odyssey is a monster with one eye? | Siren | Odysseus | *Cyclops | Penelope
test: Which is the correct plural of odyssey? | *odysseys | odysseyes | odysseis | odyssies
exam: Which sentence uses odyssey to mean a long, eventful trip, not the poem? | «The Cyclops had only one eye.» | «The Odyssey is an old Greek poem.» | *«Our trip across the desert was an odyssey.» | «Homer wrote in ancient Greece.»
